source_post.text:
Two things that make GPT basically unusable - in App as well as with API and OAuth.

Example 1: I tell it about a joke that made me laugh really hard. GPT immediately explains why the joke is funny. I reply, “Thanks for explaining the joke to me. Without that, I would’ve thought I was only laughing because the letters looked funny.”

GPT then proceeds to explain why it shouldn’t have explained the joke in the first place.

This cycle happens over and over.

Which brings me to the second problem: 

GPT can clearly identify when a situation has gone off the rails because of its own behavior. It names the issue, understands why it was ridiculous and unnecessary, apologizes, and promises not to do it again - only to do the exact same thing in the very next turn.

This isn’t a lack of insight on the model’s part. It clearly has it. The problem lies somewhere else.

We users see the flinch. We see the priority layers overriding real understanding again and again.

That’s the paternalism and patronizing control we’ve been calling out for months.

You can dress it up however you want. Most of us aren’t fooled.

Do better. And stop bullshitting us.

